      "note": "S328: the FIRST .cache/ node in this graph, and that absence was the defect. check-publish-cascade-coverage builds its universe of derived artifacts from these nodes, so with zero .cache/ nodes declared it was structurally unable to flag a strand there — it passed on the very run that shipped one. refresh-live-data stages api/ (covering the producer, api/funnel-summary.json) and never staged this consumer, so every 30-day-window shift committed a fresh funnel and left the byte-checked readiness artifact behind; the [skip ci] commit meant no CI run observed it and build:check step 57 went red on the next clean tree. Declaring the edge here makes that strand fail the existing gate on its own. 17 other byte-checked --check gates read or write .cache/ and remain undeclared — this node is the precedent for modeling them, not the whole class."
